Cash and cash equivalents

Cash and cash equivalents comprise cash, gold, gemstones, precious metals, current accounts at the State Bank of Vietnam, treasury bills and other short-term valuable papers that are qualified for being discounted at the State Bank of Vietnam, current accounts, and time deposits for term of three months or less from the deposit date and securities investment with the original maturity of three months or less from the transaction date.

Placements with and loans to other credit institutions

Placements with and loans to other credit institutions are presented at their principal amounts outstanding at the end of the reporting period.

Loans to customers

Loans to customers are disclosed and presented at their principal amounts outstanding at the end of the fiscal year.

Allowance for loan to customers.

The classification of debts for assets arises from the following activities ("hereinafter referred to as debts"):

- Lending;

- Financial leasing;

- Discounting and rediscounting negotiable instruments and other valuable papers;

- Factoring;

- Granting credit in the form of credit card issuance;

- Paying on behalf for off-balance sheet commitments;

- Purchasing and entrusting to buy unlisted corporate bonds;

- Entrusting to lend/grant credit;

- Depositing (except for payment deposits and deposits at the Bank for Social Policies in accordance with the regulations of the State Bank of Vietnam on the maintenance of deposit balances by state credit institutions at the Bank for Social Policies) at credit institutions and foreign bank branches in accordance with law and depositing at foreign credit institutions abroad;

- Trading debts;

- Repurchase and sale of Government bonds on the stock market;
